{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "name": "Titanium.UI.EmailDialog",
  "kind": "view",
  "extends": "Titanium.UI.View",
  "inheritanceChain": [
    "Titanium.UI.View",
    "Titanium.Proxy"
  ],
  "platforms": [
    "android",
    "iphone",
    "ipad",
    "macos"
  ],
  "since": "0.8",
  "summary": "An email dialog is a modal window that allows users to compose and send an email.\n",
  "description": "| Android | iOS |\n| ------- | --- |\n| ![Android](./emaildialog_android.png) | ![iOS](./emaildialog_ios.png) |\n\nThe Email Dialog is created with the [Titanium.UI.createEmailDialog](api:Titanium.UI#createEmailDialog) method. The user needs to\nregister an e-mail account on the device in order to open the dialog.  The dialog will not\nopen when there is not a registered e-mail account.\n\n**iOS Platform Notes**\n\nOn iOS, you cannot test the e-mail dialog on the iOS Simulator. Test the email dialog on device.\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Simple Email Dialog with Attachment",
      "code": "Create and send an email with a file attachment.\n\n``` js\nvar emailDialog = Ti.UI.createEmailDialog()\nemailDialog.subject = \"Hello from Titanium\";\nemailDialog.toRecipients = ['foo@yahoo.com'];\nemailDialog.messageBody = '<b>Titanium SDK Rocks!</b>';\nvar f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile('cricket.wav');\nemailDialog.addAttachment(f);\nemailDialog.open();\n```\n"
    }
  ],
